<section>
    <h3>The comment that changed the direction</h3>
    <blockquote class="review">
        We do want record and replay in HttpClient […]
        <b>build on what is already there instead of alongside it.</b>
        <br><br>
        None of this is a rejection of the idea. It is a request to make the recorder produce real HAR
        that our existing reader consumes, to <b>fail closed</b>, and to <b>keep secrets out of files people commit</b>.
        <cite>Nicolas Grekas, August 17, 2026</cite>
    </blockquote>
    <aside class="notes">
        <p>On August 17, Nicolas Grekas posted this comment.</p>
        <p>Roughly: yes, we want this feature. But build on what exists, not next to it. Real HAR, that the existing reader can read back. A replay that never goes to the network by surprise. And no secrets in committed files.</p>
        <p>That kind of comment can sting at first. But those three points are exactly the common threads of everything you've seen today. This comment became the specification of the final version.</p>
    </aside>
</section>
